# Test projects a change makes compile: programs the compiler refused before
# the change and builds after it (a program it built and ran wrong goes in
# tests/started-passing).  One per line, the project's directory name under
# tests/tests/projects, then the reason:
#
#     chain_default_param_conflict a generic parameter's type is its declaration's
#
# `make verify ARGS="--baseline REV"` applies the lines this file carries and
# REV's copy does not.  For each it asserts that REV's compiler refuses the
# project with an error diagnostic, that the compiler under test builds it, and
# that the baseline's test census fails on exactly these projects.  Their
# objects are left out of the comparison: the baseline's are only what it
# compiled before refusing (dependencies, typically), so there is no program
# on its side to compare against.  A line stays once committed: against a
# later baseline it is inert, against an earlier one it is asserted again.
generic_receiver_by_type a method whose receiver is written as one instantiation of its generic owner is specialized for the owner instantiations that are that type, compared as types: one written for B's `Point` is no longer specialized for A's (E0204 at a field only B's has), and one written for `Wrapper<i32>` or `Wrapper<Box2<i32>>` exists on it (E0358 before)
generic_function_type_argument a function type returning a pointer or an array is a generic argument like any other; its printed text ending in `*` or `[]` made it a pointer or an array, an unresolvable instantiation (E0900)
generic_function_named_like_type a generic function or static method sharing its name with a type is specialized with every name in its signature and body that resolves to the type still meaning the type; the name's spelling matched the template's and was rewritten to the function's specialization (E0200 "expected 'Tag', found 'Tag<i32>'")
class_inherited_function_field_call a call through a function-typed field a class inherits from its base finds the field as a `.field` read does, through the base chain; the call path searched only the receiver's own fields (E0358 "no method named `cb` found on type `main::B`")
supertrait_methods_through_bound a supertrait is a trait reference as a bound writes one, so `type trait Ranked : cmp::Ord` names `Ord` through its module, where the parser took a bare identifier only and the program was a cascade of E0100 parse errors
path_call_generic_method a generic method called through a path with its receiver first, `Q::go(&q, 7)` or `(BetaG for NgTf)::go(&g, 7)`, binds its own type parameters and runs its specialization, where the call named the unspecialized template (E0636, or LLVM "Incorrect number of arguments") or the path took another specialization's return type (E0200)
bound_call_through_index_field_projection a call a generic body writes on a bounded parameter reached through an index (`this.ptr[i].equals(value)`), a field of an instantiation (`node.key.equals(key)`) or a projection (`value.compare(&best)` under `where This::Item: Ord`) names the bound's method, where it was re-selected by name and refused (E0156 `equals`/`compare` is both an inherent method of `Q` and provided by a trait) for a type with both
bound_path_names_declaring_trait a path through a bounded parameter, `T::make()`, names the member of the bound whose trait or supertrait declares it (`where T: Beta + Named`, `where T: Sub` with `Sub : Gamma`), where only a parameter with exactly one bound was directed, to that bound's own trait, and both were refused at the instantiation (E0156 "`make` is provided by more than one trait implemented for `P`")
impl_qualified_path_in_generic_method a path naming a trait implementation's generic method on a concrete type, `(Bb for S)::go(&this.s, w)`, written inside a generic body with the body's own type parameter as an argument, runs that method's specialization for each instantiation, where the call named the unspecialized template (E0636 "codegen: cannot resolve 'S::go'")
trait_method_through_field_in_generic_body a trait implementation's generic method called on a concrete receiver reached through a field, `this.s.go(w)` or `t.s.go(w)`, inside a generic body runs its specialization for each instantiation, where the call named the unspecialized template (E0900 "LLVM reports: Incorrect number of arguments passed to called function!")
import_type_and_function_same_leaf a type and a function of one leaf imported from two modules bind in their own namespaces; the second import was recorded as a tie with the first whatever their namespaces (E0154 at every use, E0231 at the call)
import_alias_binds_same_item an import entry takes `as` and binds its declaration under the alias, and `import A::B as C;` names the item `B` of `A` when no module is `A::B`; a brace import of an overloaded function binds every overload (it was E0243 at the one entry), where the brace alias was a parse error (E0100) and the single form E0500
